LOCAL PATCH -- this is NOT upstream's generated parser.

  grammar.js.patch, beside this file, is applied to upstream's grammar.js
  at the rev above (sha256 09e8576d391543ae97934181ee6a5d07064c276e497abb7005129bc1ee9cd0ac).
  It adds the just 1.51 syntax upstream lacks, every hunk marked
  `LOCAL PATCH (xenolith)`:

    - `f"…"`, `f'…'`, `f"""…"""`, `f'''…'''` format strings, their
      `{{…}}` interpolation nodes inside the one `string` node;
    - `x"…"`, `x'…'`, `x"""…"""`, `x'''…'''` shell-expanded strings;
    - `&&` and `||` in expressions;
    - `assert(CONDITION, EXPRESSION)`;
    - `eager NAME := …` and attributes on an assignment (`[private]`),
      plain or exported;
    - `unexport NAME`.

  `eager` and `unexport` parse as identifiers, not keywords, so a
  variable of either name still parses. `[arg("n", pattern='\d+')]`
  already parsed at the rev above; `pattern="\d+"` is rejected by just
  1.51 itself (`\d` is no escape), so it stays a parse error.

